From 29598b43d50aed8a75009093c3ac1e420adbf914 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bitzek <erik.bitzek@googlemail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] fix mc/sites: check keyword (per-block consistency
 verification) + reset_timestep-safe block schedule

Two follow-ups from the 8B viper session (2026-07-27):

- New optional keyword 'check yes': after every MC block verify (1) global
  atom count == sum of per-rank nlocal, (2) species-atom count == catalogue
  occupancy, (3) in gc mode, the stored Metropolis reference energy against
  a fresh full-energy evaluation.  Errors out at the first inconsistent
  block; costs one extra full-energy evaluation per block.  Debug aid for
  qualifying large rank counts, new potentials, or modified builds.

- init() re-arms next_reneighbor when the scheduled first block is in the
  past or beyond the next Nevery window: a reset_timestep issued after the
  fix definition could previously disarm the fix for an entire run
  (observed as Msites=0/natt=0 in the original 8B bench input).

Docs updated (keyword, defaults, prose paragraph).
